            "size": -1,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"type\":\"data\",\"nodes\":[{\"type\":\"skip\"},{\"type\":\"skip\"},{\"type\":\"data\",\"data\":[{\"query\":1,\"user\":2,\"results\":9},\"Harry\",{\"id\":3,\"name\":4,\"email\":5,\"isAdmin\":6,\"createdAt\":7,\"updatedAt\":8},\"fb82ba91-0195-4e3e-a7c9-349791472a2a\",\"Test\",\"test@mail.com\",true,[\"Date\",\"2026-04-15T12:42:29.947Z\"],[\"Date\",\"2026-04-15T12:42:29.947Z\"],[10,18,23,28,33,38,43,48,54,60],{\"openLibraryId\":11,\"title\":12,\"author\":13,\"description\":14,\"publishedYear\":15,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL61027601M\",\"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone\",\"J. K. Rowling\",\"Il signore e la signora Dursley, di Privet Drive numero 4, erano orgogliosi di poter affermare che erano perfettamente normali, e grazie tante. Erano le ultime persone al mondo da cui aspettarsi che avessero a che fare con cose strane o misteriose, perché sciocchezze del genere proprio non le approvavano.\",1997,false,null,{\"openLibraryId\":19,\"title\":20,\"author\":13,\"description\":21,\"publishedYear\":22,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL26378158M\",\"Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows\",\"Les deux hommes surgirent de nulle part, à quelques mètres l’un de l’autre, sur le chemin étroit éclairé par la lune. Pendant un instant, ils restèrent parfaitement immobiles, chacun pointant sa baguette magique sur la poitrine de l’autre.\",2007,{\"openLibraryId\":24,\"title\":25,\"author\":13,\"description\":26,\"publishedYear\":27,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL25683482M\",\"Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire\",\"The villagers of Little Hangleton still called it “the Riddle\\r\\nHouse,” even though it had been many years since the Riddle family had lived there.\",2000,{\"openLibraryId\":29,\"title\":30,\"author\":13,\"description\":31,\"publishedYear\":32,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL26234270M\",\"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban\",\"À bien des égards, Harry Potter était un garçon des plus singuliers. Tout d’abord, il détestait les vacances d’été, c’était la période de l’année la plus déplaisante à ses yeux. Ensuite, il tenait absolument à faire ses devoirs de vacances, mais il était obligé de les faire en secret, au beau milieu de la nuit. Enfin, il faut également signaler que Harry Potter était un sorcier.\",1999,{\"openLibraryId\":34,\"title\":35,\"author\":13,\"description\":36,\"publishedYear\":37,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL59041259M\",\"Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets\",\"Ce n’était pas la première fois qu’une dispute éclatait au petit déjeuner dans la maison du 4, Privet Drive. Mr Vernon Dursley avait été réveillé à l’aube par un hululement sonore qui provenait de la chambre de son neveu Harry.\",1998,{\"openLibraryId\":39,\"title\":40,\"author\":13,\"description\":41,\"publishedYear\":42,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL61362457M\",\"Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince\",\"Il était près de minuit et le Premier Ministre, assis seul dans son bureau, lisait un long rapport dont les mots lui traversaient l’esprit sans qu’il parvienne à en saisir le moindre sens.\",2005,{\"openLibraryId\":44,\"title\":45,\"author\":13,\"description\":46,\"publishedYear\":47,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL25662116M\",\"Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix\",\"Il giorno più caldo dell’estate – almeno fino a quel momento – volgeva al termine e un silenzio sonnacchioso gravava sulle grandi case quadrate di Privet Drive.\",2003,{\"openLibraryId\":49,\"title\":50,\"author\":51,\"description\":52,\"publishedYear\":53,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL12761348M\",\"Der Steppenwolf\",\"Hermann Hesse\",\"The day had gone by just as days go by.\",1927,{\"openLibraryId\":55,\"title\":56,\"author\":57,\"description\":58,\"publishedYear\":59,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL23348263M\",\"Three Men in a Boat (to say nothing of the dog)\",\"Jerome Klapka Jérôme\",\"Three Invalids-Sufferings of George and Harris.\",1889,{\"openLibraryId\":61,\"title\":62,\"author\":63,\"description\":64,\"publishedYear\":65,\"onShelf\":16,\"shelfEntryId\":17,\"rating\":17},\"OL12587028M\",\"Бѣсы\",\"Фёдор Михайлович Достоевский\",\"IN setting out to describe the recent and very strange events that occurred in our hitherto completely undistinguished little town, I am compelled by my own lack of talent to begin from some time back, that is, with a few biographical details about the talented and highly esteemed Stepan Trofimovich Verkhovensky.\",1871],\"uses\":{\"search_params\":[\"query\"]}}]}\n"
